; A table whose DOMAIN is a NAMED recursive union, with the cycle rooted at the UNION so the table
; registers FIRST — `u_holder = [u_val]` makes dep ordering register `u_map` while `u_val` is still
; nothing. `register_rust_struct` cannot name the keys-list wasm wrapper from such a domain
; (`name_as_wasm_array_ct` -> `directly_wasm_exposable_ct` -> `is_enum`, whose registered-or-generic
; assertion is right to fire on an ident in neither map), so the mint is DEFERRED to
; `finalize_deferred_table_keys_lists`, which names it from the by-then-final domain — the same route
; a generic-collection-instance domain already took. This row is the OUTCOME half of that fix: it
; asserts the ordering generates at all, under the catalog's default flags.
;
; The behavioural halves live beside it: the mint/reference agreement and the `--wasm=false` leg in
; `union_rooted_recursive_union_keyed_table_mints_its_keys_list`, the compile-and-wire floor in the
; `ukey_`/`upres_` blocks of tests/recursive-collection-ref/input.cddl (both profiles), and the
; collection-rooted twin — the ordering that mints at registration time — in that fixture's `key_`
; block with `recursive_union_keyed_table_mints_its_keys_list_under_wasm`.
u_holder = [u_val]
u_val = u_map / int / bytes / text
u_map = { * u_val => u_val }
